.TH DEVTEST 1
.SH NAME
mouse, mousedev, ptrcheck, irtest, progstem_probe \- device/driver diagnostic tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mouse
.RI [ type ]
.br
.B mousedev
.br
.B ptrcheck
.br
.B irtest
.br
.B progstem_probe
.SH DESCRIPTION
Small developer diagnostics for hardware and kernel device support,
not general end-user tools. Each writes a plain-text report of what it
found (most to
.B /tmp
or standard output) rather than presenting a UI.
.PP
.TP
.B mouse
Ported from Plan 9's
.BR aux/mouse :
initializes a serial mouse of the given
.IR type
(probing standard speeds if none given) and relays its events onto
.BR /dev/mouse .
.TP
.B mousedev
Opens the display and
.BR /dev/pointer ,
then logs the first 30 raw pointer events read from it to
.BR /tmp/mousedev.out .
.TP
.B ptrcheck
Checks that
.B /dev/pointer
and
.B /dev/cursor
both open successfully (logging the result to
.BR /tmp/ptrcheck.out ,
or standard error if that can't be created), then hands off to
.IR wm (1).
.TP
.B irtest
Exercises the infrared device driver
.RI ( ir.m ),
loading it from either its normal or simulator path.
.TP
.B progstem_probe
Reads its own
.B /prog/<pid>/{text,status,heap,stack}
files and prints each one's metadata and a sample of its content \(em
a smoke test for the
.B /prog
per-process filesystem.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/mouse.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/mousedev.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/ptrcheck.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/irtest.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/progstem_probe.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wm (1)
